      "side": 1,
      "message": "Typedefs to arrays always scare me, because arrays do not have the same semantics as other types; e.g. they are always passed by reference. And you have to include the top-level const in the type, which has advantages but makes things even less obvious at the point of use.\n\nHow about\n```\ntypedef struct path_alts_t {\n  const char* paths[MAX_CONTEXT_PATHS][MAX_ALT_CONTEXT_PATHS];\n} path_alts_t;\n```\n\nWhich avoids both problems? Then pass a pointer to this struct - which doesn\u0027t introduce any inefficiency.",
